<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Near Field Communication Tag Reading.

	  Required before Core NFC will start a session at all: without this entitlement on
	  the provisioning profile, startScanning() fails at runtime on a real device even
	  though the code, the plugin and Info.plist are all correct. The failure looks like
	  a bug in the app rather than a missing capability, which is why it is written down
	  here rather than left to be rediscovered.

	  TAG, NOT NDEF — and this reverses a deliberate choice, so the reason is recorded.

	  It used to read NDEF only, on the argument that a raw tag session reads the chip
	  directly and is a broader permission than reading a check-in sticker warrants.
	  That argument was sound and is now moot: Apple's upload validator refuses it. A
	  binary built against the current SDK with a minimum of iOS 15 is rejected at
	  App Store Connect with error 90778, saying both halves plainly —

	      'TAG is missing in the entitlement'
	      'NDEF is disallowed'

	  So the narrow option no longer exists. NDEF is not a format we may ask for any
	  more, and TAG is the only value that uploads at all. Reading an NDEF message off
	  a sticker still works through it; what changed is the name of the permission we
	  have to hold to do it, not what the app does with the tag.

	  Found at the UPLOAD step, not at build: the archive compiled and signed cleanly
	  and was rejected afterwards by App Store Connect, which is why it survived every
	  local check.

	  THIS FILE IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. Two manual steps remain, in Xcode:
	    1. Signing & Capabilities -> + Capability -> Near Field Communication Tag Reading
	       (this writes the matching entry into the App target's build settings, and
	       regenerates the provisioning profile with the capability enabled).
	    2. Confirm the App target's CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS points at this file.
	  A build that skips those will compile, install, and then refuse every scan.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats</key>
	<array>
		<string>TAG</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
